{"skill":{"slug":"xhs-cover-skill","displayName":"Xhs Cover Skill"},"version":{"version":"3.0.0","createdAt":1775748863191,"changelog":"改用 npx xhscover，支持终端内注册登录，移除手动 API Key 配置","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3067,"sha256":"aaf774126828df47c99dd60167ea3f71ed1aa84ccef1fd68173fb9e97f2ca079","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1600,"sha256":"a52f540f667f16764d1f16c654d9e1ad79183283723996bb9a05d76ef867bb7b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","size":160,"sha256":"9fc561c895ca4f25497308abe6ed529be3146f12d0039d9fd0826cbb1ef7adaa","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1976,"sha256":"e81ae8d14957cf9be8aa26c0a47b44ce9d0e48af696d3e74bc2c7ddeb919c2f7","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789107087276,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5e9522fc0d903c2ced69d40a121646d6c5d43a8e16ad8c212f91eedd5c8f93eb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5e9522fc0d903c2ced69d40a121646d6c5d43a8e16ad8c212f91eedd5c8f93eb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085719797},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":35,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":17,"checkedAt":1789107087276},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill appears purpose-aligned, but it repeatedly runs an unpinned npm CLI that can change after review while handling an API key and user-provided content.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Running a mutable npm package through npx gives third-party code local user-level execution while the workflow also uses a saved API key and sends prompts to api.xhscover.cn.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill and wrapper use `npx xhscover` without an exact version, lockfile, or integrity control, so the code executed at runtime is not fixed by the reviewed artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Activation covers cover/image generation plus credit and history requests; this is somewhat broad for a remote service but still related to the stated purpose.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The README says the API key is saved under `~/.xhscover`; no evidence shows system services, scheduled tasks, privilege escalation, or hidden persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Xiaohongshu/social cover generation, balance checks, and history lookup; those capabilities match the README and SKILL.md, and the remote API data flow is disclosed.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing. The main issue is not hidden malicious code in the skill package, but that normal use runs the latest `xhscover` package from npm unless you pin or preinstall a trusted version. Only use it if you trust the xhscover npm package and xhscover.cn service with your API key and cover text.","findings":"[RP1] unexpected: Confirmed as a material concern: using an external CLI is purpose-aligned, but repeatedly resolving `xhscover` through unpinned `npx` is not necessary for the cover-generation purpose and leaves runtime behavior mutable.\n[T08] unexpected: Confirmed: `artifact/scripts/xhs-cover.sh` directly executes `npx xhscover \"$@\"`; argument passing is quoted, and no embedded malicious script was found, but dependency execution is unconstrained.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded: the activation language is broad, but it remains centered on cover generation, balances, and history; the skill discloses that API key and cover text are sent to the remote service.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: Chinese-language documentation and examples fit a Xiaohongshu-focused cover generator and do not by themselves indicate unsafe behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789107087276}}}}}